Remove the first of two identical zookeeper dependencyManagement entries.

The tika-parent pom declares org.apache.zookeeper:zookeeper twice in
dependencyManagement (once in the general section, once for the Solr 8
emitter), both resolving to ${zookeeper.version}. Maven >= 3.10 rejects
duplicate dependencies as a model validation error. Removing the first
declaration keeps the commented one and does not change resolution, as
both pick the same version.
---
--- a/tika-parent/pom.xml
+++ b/tika-parent/pom.xml
@@ -496,11 +496,6 @@
         <version>6.4.1</version>
       </dependency>
       <dependency>
-        <groupId>org.apache.zookeeper</groupId>
-        <artifactId>zookeeper</artifactId>
-        <version>${zookeeper.version}</version>
-      </dependency>
-      <dependency>
         <groupId>com.amazonaws</groupId>
         <artifactId>aws-java-sdk-s3</artifactId>
         <version>${aws.version}</version>
